        {
            "id": "044dadfb-16ac-497e-bbf5-c8749d16c284",
            "build_id": "9d4e3007-650f-4145-8042-69dd3852ce9e",
            "round_number": 4,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-08-19T12:49:20.064295+00:00",
            "notes": "[Superflexor](item_580b77b4-0d63-469b-99a8-5372c55dfc1b) is going to be a huge amount of value if you're able to afford it. For the cost, it gives you a crazy amount of AP that's easy to keep up with Soldier. It's also part of the reason to try to land a few weapon shots before firing your rockets, when you're able.\n\nIf you don't have the cash yet, just fill your slots out with optional blues (and greens, if needed) for now, and re-adjust next round. If you're just shy of being able to afford it, and the enemy team has a fair amount of armor, [Codebreaker](item_caa96c7e-655f-4d03-9bd9-0f41937fec27) can be a solid pick. At $9K, it gives the same amount of weapon power as [Talon Modification Module](item_c0ca1795-a3ea-4dc9-ae17-f34122574b3a), so it's like getting the 50% less armor damage reduction for just another $3K without needing another item slot. It's tricky to try to quantify *exactly* how valuable the 50% less armor damage reduction is, but it's big, especially for heroes like Soldier 76 that deal many instances of light damage. Armor typically makes up ~40-50% of the health of armor-bearing tanks like Reinhardt, Orisa, or D.Va, and can be as high or higher for squishier targets that frequently pick up [Vital-E-Tee](item_b92e6f1d-3aac-4eec-b027-00c8e1529016), like Mei, Lucio, Genji, Reaper, or Zenyatta. Taking armor down faster isn't just a boost to your damage, but can also help turn the tide of battles by helping your teammates do more damage once the enemy's HP is below the armor threshold.",
